{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-199275-r4599163","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Memphis-Style BBQ Ribs","sourcePageId":199275,"sourceRevision":"4599163","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-11-10T02:52:26Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Memphis-Style%20BBQ%20Ribs&oldid=4599163","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:29.501Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Barbecue recipes","Category:Grilled recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using molasses","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Southern U.S. recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"bc0eb526c28bc94ede9fad38bb950d13f19089087976a553bc8d6f2b7f5620bf","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Pork recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThis is a classic U.S. style of BBQ pork ribs.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 slab [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] spareribs\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Rib Rub|Rib Rub]]                                           \n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Molasses|molasses]]\n* ¼ cup apple [[Cookbook:Cider Vinegar|cider vinegar]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* Hickory chunks\n\n==Procedure==\n#Season spareribs with rib rub.\n#Refrigerate for at least 1 hour.\n#Place chunks in smoker or charcoal [[Cookbook:Grill|grill]] set for indirect heat at 250°F (120°C).\n#Combine liquid ingredients and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] over high heat.\n#Reduce liquid by ⅓.\n#Place spareribs into smoker or grill for 4–5 hours, [[Cookbook:Basting|basting]] occasionally with sauce.\n#[[Cookbook:Brush|Brush]] remaining sauce on top of ribs and place on a medium-high grill until browned. The internal temperature of the ribs before removing from the grill needs to be at least 145°F (63°C).\n#Let rest for 10 minutes, covered, and carve.\n\n\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Barbecue recipes]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using molasses]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Memphis-Style BBQ Ribs","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 slab pork spareribs","sourceText":"1 slab pork spareribs","amountText":"1 slab pork spareribs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"6 tbsp Rib Rub","sourceText":"6 tbsp Rib Rub","amountText":"6 tbsp Rib Rub","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 cup tomato paste","sourceText":"1 cup tomato paste","amountText":"1 cup tomato paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ cup molasses","sourceText":"½ cup molasses","amountText":"½ cup molasses","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"¼ cup apple cider vinegar","sourceText":"¼ cup apple cider vinegar","amountText":"¼ cup ap